Package: com.albrhi.panel
Name: Albrhi Panel (rootless)
Version: 0.2.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: See which tweaks are changing which apps, from Settings.
 .
 Your package manager knows what is installed. Nothing on the phone tells you what is
 actually running inside which app. Albrhi Panel does.
 .
 It adds a page to the iOS Settings app listing every app a tweak is changing, and every
 tweak on the device with the apps it reaches. The list is read from each tweak's own
 filter file, so it shows what is really loaded rather than what a package claims.
 .
 ▍TURN ALBRHI OFF FOR ONE APP
 Tap an app and switch Albrhi off inside it, without uninstalling anything. Your settings
 are kept and come back when you switch it on again. Close and reopen the app for the
 change to take effect.
 .
 Tweaks by other developers are listed but cannot be switched from here yet — that needs a
 part of the system this version does not touch. Nothing is ever moved or deleted.
 .
 Arabic and English.
 .
